==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|frm|en}} {{term|tendrillon||bud, shoot, cartilage|lang=frm}}, perhaps a diminutive of {{term|tendron||cartilage|lang=frm}}, from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|tendre||soft|lang=fro}} (see [[tender]] (adj.)), or else from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|tendere||to stretch, extend|lang=la}} (see [[tender]] (v.)).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈtɛn.dɹəl/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|botany|lang=en}} A thin, [[spirally]] [[coiling]] [[stem]] that attaches a [[plant]] to its [[support]].
# {{context|zoology|lang=en}} A [[hair]]-like [[tentacle]].

